    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d498">

                <pb facs="0560" n="548" sameAs="frus:frus1943v05/pg548"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">740.0011 European War 1939/29104: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Bolivia</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Boal</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">La
                                Paz</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1943-04-21T13:00:00-04:00">April 21, 1943—1
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received 3:20 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>769. Department’s 578, April 20, 3 p.m.,<anchor n="39" xml:id="d498-f1"/> and
                    566, April 16, midnight. Exchange of notes based on Department’s telegrams under
                    reference but specifying “Nations of the Axis” instead of Germany, Italy and
                    Japan is being prepared for signature tomorrow April 22 at noon.</p>
                <p>After exchange of notes the Foreign Minister plans to issue a press statement to
                    the effect that Bolivia has signified its adherence to the United Nations
                    Declaration by a note; that this adherence has been acknowledged by means of a
                    note; and that President Peñaranda will sign the Declaration while in
                        Washington.<anchor n="40" xml:id="d498-f2"/></p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Boal</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d498-f1" n="39" xml:id="d498-f1-content">
                <p>Not printed.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d498-f2" n="40" xml:id="d498-f2-content">
                <p>The signed copy of Bolivia’s adherence was transmitted to the Department by the
                    Ambassador in his despatch No. 1583, April 27, 1943; received May 6.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
